{comment: Verse 1}
[C]One bright day [G7]we will [C]be caught up [C7/E]in the sky home
We will [F]enter through tho[C]se pearl gates
For they [D7]stand open [G7]wide
All of our [C]heartache and tho[G7]se troubles too
Will [C]be out [C7]of  mi[F]nd
For [C]heaven will [G7]be our ne[C]w home[F/G]

{comment: Chorus}
I'm [C]determin[C/E]ed to mak[F]e heaven [C]my   [G7]home[C]
[F/G]I'm   d[C]etermined to [D7]see those stree[G]ts   [G7]of gold
To see the [C]lion [C7]lay by the [F]lamb
To [C]sit  [C7]at my Master'[F]s scarred hands
I'm deter[C]mined to make [G7]heaven [C]my home

{comment: Verse 2}
{ci: (raise 1/2 step)}
Joy and peace, deliverance, victory shall be mine
For the blood of Christ gave me the hope
To tell this old world good-bye
I have a mansion there
A clean robe to wear
This promise it is mine
When I make heaven make heaven my home

{comment: Chorus 2}
I'm determined to make heaven my  home
I'm   determined to see those streets  of gold
To see the lion lay by the lamb
To sit at my Master's scarred hands
I'm determined
I'm determined
I'm determined to make heaven my home
